Individual nurses, doctors, and other clinicians hand collect physical notes;
These notes are aggregated into counts of disease, giving us an idea (but not strict confirmation) of prevalence;
This therefore constitutes count data; as such, we assume that NAs in a particular category represent zero-counts for that disease for that time period.

0.3 Current curation boundary
The repository is ready to establish infrastructure and orchestration, but the following scientific decisions are intentionally not encoded yet:

the authoritative source files and their provenance;
the unit of observation and stable identifiers;
the boundary between pre-DHIS2 and post-DHIS2 processing;
missing-value and zero-count semantics by field and era;
validation rules, disclosure controls, and release schema;
the release version and publication destination.

Those decisions belong in the Pipeline pages after review by a data steward and domain expert. Rendering this Manual never opens files under data/.

This project concerns private health data. Repository access and FASRC storage controls are necessary but do not decide what may enter a release.
Before source inspection or curation begins, a human data steward must record:

the authoritative source location and custodian;
whether files contain direct or quasi-identifiers;
approved users and computational locations;
permissible row- and geography-level release grain;
masking, aggregation, and small-cell rules;
retention and deletion requirements;
the reviewer who authorizes publication.

These are scientific and governance decisions, not infrastructure defaults. Until they are recorded, Pipeline pages deliberately stop at inventory and scaffolding. Do not include values, screenshots, tables, or summaries derived from protected data in the rendered Manual.

Release packaging begins only after curated targets and disclosure rules are approved. This page deliberately chooses no format, schema, version, or destination yet.






Important Prerequisite: Approve The Release Contract



A human owner must decide:

release resources and their grain;
public, restricted, or internal access classification;
allowed identifiers, geographies, and temporal resolution;
required data dictionaries and provenance metadata;
validation standard and publication destination;
semantic version and immutability policy.









Tip Procedure: Package Without Re-Cleaning



Future package targets should consume curated targets, attach reviewed schema and provenance, write to a versioned directory under data/processed, and refuse to overwrite a nonempty immutable release. Packaging must not contain a second, hidden implementation of cleaning rules.
