# release_package_validated_list &lt;- { ... }
# release_files_published_paths &lt;- { ... }








Warning Check: Verify Release Evidence



Future checks must validate the package schema, disclosure controls, round-trip equality with curated targets, provenance, checksums, and a no-op second targets run.

There is no release to verify during scaffolding. This page defines the evidence boundary that the future release implementation must satisfy.






Important Prerequisite: Confirm Release Completion



The versioned release target must have completed, and the approving reviewer must identify the exact release directory and expected resources.








Tip Procedure: Validate The Published Artifact



Future verification must:

load the published artifact through its declared interchange format;
validate every resource against its schema;
confirm identifiers and prohibited fields are absent;
compare published resources with their curated targets;
record package versions, source provenance, checksums, and review approval;
run the pipeline again and confirm that no target rebuilds.

Verification code belongs here only after the release contract is approved.








Warning Check: Retain Reproducible Evidence



Store non-disclosive verification output with the release record. Never include protected rows or values in the rendered Manual, scheduler logs, or version control.
